invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_avx512.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20_avx512.c drops the target attribute that turns AVX-512F on
  for its own functions, so the kernel compiles only where the whole object
  is built with -mavx512f, and an object built that way runs AVX-512 in
  code the caller's CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA bit never chose. The script
  compiles the file for x86-64 with no instruction flag and requires the
  kernel on 512-bit registers.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx512f"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("avx512f")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
